Next, to get the average capacity, I can use the AVG() function. So I'll modify the query to include that: SELECT AVG(Capacity) FROM stadium;

For the maximum capacity, I think I need to use the MAX() function. So the query would be SELECT MAX(Capacity) FROM stadium;

Putting it all together, I can write a single SQL query that selects both the average and the maximum capacity. I'll make sure to use semicolons to separate each statement and a comma after the first to combine them into one query.

I should also mention that the data in the Stadium table must have a Capacity column with numeric values, as SQLite might throw an error otherwise. But since the user is asking for this, I assume the data is correct.

So the final query will select all capacities, then the average, and then the maximum. I'll present this in a code block as the answer.
